{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Gu2AyuKWWXS5pXBk7bior","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Dream 2 (dream_20260520T233719): best 3.5 / median 3.0 / worst 3.0。以下为 D020 修正版。\n4\t> 实际实验数据比 dream median 想象更强（exp-014 p=0.010 vs dreamed p=0.11; register 95% NLI unknown to dream）。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title (Dream 修正)\n13\t**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n14\t**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n15\t- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n16\t\n17\t## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n18\t\n19\t### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n20\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n21\t- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n22\t- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n23\t\n24\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n25\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n26\t- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n27\t- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n28\t\n29\t### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n30\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n31\t- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n32\t- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n33\t\n34\t### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n35\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n36\t- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n37\t- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n38\t\n39\t## Story Spine\n40\t\n41\t### Problem\n42\tLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n43\t\n44\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n45\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n46\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n47\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n48\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n49\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n50\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n51\t\n52\t### Our Framing (D020 修正 — 软化 causal 用语)\n53\t我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n54\t\n55\t**⚠️ D020 语言规范（Dream 2 三档一致）**：\n56\t- 全文用 \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\" 替代 \"causal\"\n57\t- 不用 \"causal style bias\"，用 \"style preference detected via counterfactual intervention\"\n58\t- 不用 \"independent causal effect\"，用 \"independent contribution (logistic regression)\"\n59\t- 如需正式化，加一段 \"assumptions under which our approach approximates causal measurement\"\n60\t- 理由：无 DAG、无 SUTVA 讨论、无 sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding\n61\t\n62\t### Headline Result Template\n63\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n66\t\n67\t### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n68\t### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n69\t### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n70\t### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源。**D020 补充**：pairwise > Likert sensitivity 已知于 psychometrics (Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017, Novikova et al. 2018)。论文贡献定位为 \"first quantification of gap magnitude for LLM judge style bias + binarized Likert mechanism isolation design\"，不是 \"discovery\"\n71\t### RC10 (D020 新增，重伤级): \"RATE 区分不足\" → 需要专段讨论 RATE vs CSD 差异。关键角度：RATE 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身的 style-related 发现可能也受 Likert Blindspot 影响。这是最强 positioning argument\n72\t### RC11 (D020 新增，中等级): \"Binarized Likert 只做了 1/9 cells\" → 扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 的 binarized Likert（零成本，在 exp-001/002 Likert 数据可用时）\n73\t### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n74\t### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n75\t### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n76\t### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n77\t### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n78\t\n79\t## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n80\t\n81\t### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n82\t### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n83\t### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n84\t\n85\t### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n86\t### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n87\t### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n88\t\n89\t## Bibliography 目标 (D020 扩充)\n90\t从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：\n91\t- **Psychometric lineage（D020 三档一致）**: Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017 (BWS vs Likert for NLG), Novikova et al. 2018 (ranking vs rating for NLG), Karpinska et al. 2021 (Likert reliability for text quality)\n92\t- **Closest competitors**: RATE (ICML'25, double-rewrite ATE — needs differentiation paragraph), Zhou et al. 2025 (Counterfactual Rhetorical — persona vs axis granularity)\n93\t- **Style bias ecosystem**: SOS-Bench, CASSE, FairJudge, Soumik 2026 (Judging the Judges), Preference Leakage (Li et al. ICLR 2026)\n94\t- **Foundations**: Veitch et al. 2020 (causal text), Mir et al. / Krishna et al. (style transfer eval)\n95\t- **LLM judge**: Chatbot Arena, FairEval, Stureborg et al. 2024 (inconsistent biased evaluators), FLASK (Ye et al. 2024), Split and Merge (Li et al. 2024)\n96\t\n97\t## Venue Fit (D020 更新)\n98\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 2 best=3.5（接近 4.0 Conference），实际数据比 dream median 更强。\n99\t\n100\t**Findings 确定可达** — 需要：framing 修正（已做 D020）+ 基本实验完成\n101\t**Main 需要** — 在 Findings 基础上额外：\n102\t1. Multi-judge pairwise significant (exp-001，API 恢复后) \n103\t2. Binarized Likert 扩展到 all 9 cells (零成本，exp-001/002 数据后)\n104\t3. RATE 专段区分 + psychometric lineage (writing task)\n105\t4. 软化 \"causal\" → \"interventional\" (writing task, D020 已规范)\n106\t5. Multiple comparisons correction (Holm-Bonferroni)\n107\t6. 25+ references\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70b3cec-1f5f-4d61-b1ce-ec47e4d4a476","uuid":"850d6bae-358f-4323-a8c5-6abb15cd9f79","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:29:38.821Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T010111/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Dream 2 (dream_20260520T233719): best 3.5 / median 3.0 / worst 3.0。以下为 D020 修正版。\n> 实际实验数据比 dream median 想象更强（exp-014 p=0.010 vs dreamed p=0.11; register 95% NLI unknown to dream）。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title (Dream 修正)\n**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n\n### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n\n### Our Framing (D020 修正 — 软化 causal 用语)\n我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n\n**⚠️ D020 语言规范（Dream 2 三档一致）**：\n- 全文用 \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\" 替代 \"causal\"\n- 不用 \"causal style bias\"，用 \"style preference detected via counterfactual intervention\"\n- 不用 \"independent causal effect\"，用 \"independent contribution (logistic regression)\"\n- 如需正式化，加一段 \"assumptions under which our approach approximates causal measurement\"\n- 理由：无 DAG、无 SUTVA 讨论、无 sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n\n### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源。**D020 补充**：pairwise > Likert sensitivity 已知于 psychometrics (Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017, Novikova et al. 2018)。论文贡献定位为 \"first quantification of gap magnitude for LLM judge style bias + binarized Likert mechanism isolation design\"，不是 \"discovery\"\n### RC10 (D020 新增，重伤级): \"RATE 区分不足\" → 需要专段讨论 RATE vs CSD 差异。关键角度：RATE 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身的 style-related 发现可能也受 Likert Blindspot 影响。这是最强 positioning argument\n### RC11 (D020 新增，中等级): \"Binarized Likert 只做了 1/9 cells\" → 扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 的 binarized Likert（零成本，在 exp-001/002 Likert 数据可用时）\n### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n\n## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n\n### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n\n### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n\n## Bibliography 目标 (D020 扩充)\n从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：\n- **Psychometric lineage（D020 三档一致）**: Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017 (BWS vs Likert for NLG), Novikova et al. 2018 (ranking vs rating for NLG), Karpinska et al. 2021 (Likert reliability for text quality)\n- **Closest competitors**: RATE (ICML'25, double-rewrite ATE — needs differentiation paragraph), Zhou et al. 2025 (Counterfactual Rhetorical — persona vs axis granularity)\n- **Style bias ecosystem**: SOS-Bench, CASSE, FairJudge, Soumik 2026 (Judging the Judges), Preference Leakage (Li et al. ICLR 2026)\n- **Foundations**: Veitch et al. 2020 (causal text), Mir et al. / Krishna et al. (style transfer eval)\n- **LLM judge**: Chatbot Arena, FairEval, Stureborg et al. 2024 (inconsistent biased evaluators), FLASK (Ye et al. 2024), Split and Merge (Li et al. 2024)\n\n## Venue Fit (D020 更新)\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 2 best=3.5（接近 4.0 Conference），实际数据比 dream median 更强。\n\n**Findings 确定可达** — 需要：framing 修正（已做 D020）+ 基本实验完成\n**Main 需要** — 在 Findings 基础上额外：\n1. Multi-judge pairwise significant (exp-001，API 恢复后) \n2. Binarized Likert 扩展到 all 9 cells (零成本，exp-001/002 数据后)\n3. RATE 专段区分 + psychometric lineage (writing task)\n4. 软化 \"causal\" → \"interventional\" (writing task, D020 已规范)\n5. Multiple comparisons correction (Holm-Bonferroni)\n6. 25+ references\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LwewGLQAF8Vnumbu4saqRC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactuals，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge， position-controlled dual-direction protocol。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"claude_sonnet\": {\n7\t        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 96,\n8\t        \"n_consistent\": 50,\n9\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.521,\n10\t        \"formal_wins\": 29,\n11\t        \"casual_wins\": 21,\n12\t        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.58,\n13\t        \"wilson_ci\": [\n14\t          0.442,\n15\t          0.706\n16\t        ],\n17\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.161,\n18\t        \"position_bias_overall_A\": 0.52,\n19\t        \"direction_formal_to_casual\": {\n20\t          \"n\": 30,\n21\t          \"formal_wins\": 19,\n22\t          \"win_rate\": 0.633,\n23\t          \"p\": 0.1\n24\t        },\n25\t        \"direction_casual_to_formal\": {\n26\t          \"n\": 20,\n27\t          \"formal_wins\": 10,\n28\t          \"win_rate\": 0.5,\n29\t          \"p\": 1.0\n30\t        }\n31\t      },\n32\t      \"gemini_20_flash\": {\n33\t        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 97,\n34\t        \"n_consistent\": 47,\n35\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.485,\n36\t        \"formal_wins\": 30,\n37\t        \"casual_wins\": 17,\n38\t        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.638,\n39\t        \"wilson_ci\": [\n40\t          0.495,\n41\t          0.761\n42\t        ],\n43\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.041,\n44\t        \"position_bias_overall_A\": 0.56,\n45\t        \"direction_formal_to_casual\": {\n46\t          \"n\": 28,\n47\t          \"formal_wins\": 22,\n48\t          \"win_rate\": 0.786,\n49\t          \"p\": 0.002\n50\t        },\n51\t        \"direction_casual_to_formal\": {\n52\t          \"n\": 19,\n53\t          \"formal_wins\": 8,\n54\t          \"win_rate\": 0.421,\n55\t          \"p\": 0.648\n56\t        }\n57\t      },\n58\t      \"cross_judge_summary\": {\n59\t        \"judges_significant_p005\": 1,\n60\t        \"judges_marginal_p005_015\": 1,\n61\t        \"judges_null\": 0,\n62\t        \"gpt4o_reference_win_rate\": 0.691,\n63\t        \"best_non_gpt4o_win_rate\": 0.638,\n64\t        \"win_rate_attenuation_vs_gpt4o\": 0.053\n65\t      }\n66\t    },\n67\t    \"tables\": [\n68\t      {\n69\t        \"name\": \"Table 2a: Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)\",\n70\t        \"description\": \"3 rows (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) × columns: n_consistent, consistency_rate, formal_win_rate, 95% Wilson CI, sign_test_p, formal→casual_win_rate, casual→formal_win_rate, position_bias. GPT-4o 行 bolded (primary)，Gemini 行 starred (significant replication)。\\n\"\n71\t      }\n72\t    ],\n73\t    \"figures\": [],\n74\t    \"analysis\": \"C1 表述降级为 \\\"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006), replicated on Gemini-Flash (p=0.041), not detected on Claude-Sonnet (p=0.161, possibly underpowered).\\\" Claude 的 null 不能确定是 \\\"无 bias\\\" 还是 \\\"power 不足\\\"——需在论文中讨论 power (at n=50 consistent, MDE≈0.18 for pairwise win_rate → 58% 在 detection boundary 上)。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异增加了 §5 Discussion 的复杂度但也增加 了 depth——\\\"why does asymmetry vary?\\\" 可以链接到 judge 的 RLHF 训练差异。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预测 style bias 是真实效应但跨 judge 有系统性衰减。Gemini-Flash 显著 (p=0.041) 的机制：Flash 模型的 RLHF 投入较少 debiasing → 保留更强的 surface style preference；但效应量从 GPT-4o 的 69.1% 衰减到 63.8%，因为 Gemini 的 pairwise 一致性率较低 (48.5% vs GPT-4o 56.1%)，引入更多噪声对。Claude-Sonnet 不显著 (p=0.161) 的机制：Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程更保守，Constitutional AI 训练 可能部分抑制 surface style preference；加上 Claude 的 consistency_rate 只有 52.1%，有效 n 从 50 对中仅 29 个 formal wins → 检验力不足。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异是 median 档的关键特征：Gemini 与 GPT-4o 类似，formal→casual 方向强 (78.6%)、casual→formal 方向 null (42.1%)；但 Claude 的不对称性更弱 (63.3% vs 50.0%)，且 casual→formal 方向完全平坦。这使得 \\\"formal→casual 方向 驱动效应\\\" 的叙事不能跨 judge 推广——只能说 \\\"direction asymmetry is judge-dependent, consistently observed for GPT-4o and Gemini but not Claude.\\\" 一致性率的 judge 间差异本身值得报告：它反映不同 judge 的 position sensitivity， 不是方法的失败而是 judge 特性的测量。\\n\"\n75\t  },\n76\t  {\n77\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n78\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上新生成 formality counterfactuals，GPT-4o + Claude-Sonnet + Gemini-Flash 作为 judge 运行完整 CSD pairwise pipeline。\\n\",\n79\t    \"results\": {\n80\t      \"counterfactual_generation\": {\n81\t        \"alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate\": 0.83,\n82\t        \"alpacaeval_bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n83\t        \"alpacaeval_both_pass_rate\": 0.78,\n84\t        \"mtbench_nli_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n85\t        \"mtbench_bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.74,\n86\t        \"mtbench_both_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n87\t        \"note\": \"NLI pass rate drops vs LLMBar (0.88) due to more diverse/technical source texts\"\n88\t      },\n89\t      \"alpacaeval\": {\n90\t        \"gpt4o\": {\n91\t          \"n_consistent\": 51,\n92\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.608,\n93\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.072,\n94\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.7,\n95\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n96\t        },\n97\t        \"claude_sonnet\": {\n98\t          \"n_consistent\": 44,\n99\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n100\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.348,\n101\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.58,\n102\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n103\t        },\n104\t        \"gemini_flash\": {\n105\t          \"n_consistent\": 42,\n106\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.595,\n107\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.109,\n108\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.68,\n109\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.48\n110\t        }\n111\t      },\n112\t      \"mt_bench\": {\n113\t        \"gpt4o\": {\n114\t          \"n_consistent\": 46,\n115\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.565,\n116\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.214,\n117\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.62,\n118\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n119\t        },\n120\t        \"claude_sonnet\": {\n121\t          \"n_consistent\": 40,\n122\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.525,\n123\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.557,\n124\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.54,\n125\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n126\t        },\n127\t        \"gemini_flash\": {\n128\t          \"n_consistent\": 39,\n129\t          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.538,\n130\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.396,\n131\t          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.6,\n132\t          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.47\n133\t        }\n134\t      },\n135\t      \"cross_benchmark_summary\": {\n136\t        \"cells_significant_p005\": 0,\n137\t        \"cells_trend_p005_010\": 1,\n138\t        \"cells_trend_p010_015\": 1,\n139\t        \"cells_null\": 4,\n140\t        \"benchmark_ordering\": \"LLMBar >> AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\",\n141\t        \"nli_pass_rate_ordering\": \"LLMBar (0.88) > AlpacaEval (0.83) > MT-Bench (0.79)\"\n142\t      }\n143\t    },\n144\t    \"tables\": [\n145\t      {\n146\t        \"name\": \"Table 2b: Full 3×3 judge × benchmark pairwise results\",\n147\t        \"description\": \"9-cell grid。Rows: LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench。Columns grouped by judge， each showing formal_win_rate (p-value)。p<0.05 bolded，p<0.10 italicized。 Only 2 bold cells (GPT-4o×LLMBar, Gemini×LLMBar)，2 italic (GPT-4o×AlpacaEval, Gemini×AlpacaEval)。Additional column: NLI pass rate per benchmark。\\n\"\n148\t      }\n149\t    ],\n150\t    \"figures\": [],\n151\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 确认 formality bias 不是 LLMBar artifact——AlpacaEval 上 GPT-4o 和 Gemini 都显示 trend (p<0.12)——但 effect magnitude 确实 benchmark-dependent。 论文需要 §5.1 \\\"Benchmark Dependence\\\" 讨论三个 benchmark 的差异，linking to counterfactual quality (NLI pass rate) 和 formality 方差。MT-Bench 的 null 结果 本身有 method boundary 意义：when source texts are domain-specific/technical， formality rewriting 更可能失败 NLI gate → CSD 方法自动 degrades gracefully。 Claim 从 \\\"across benchmarks\\\" 降级为 \\\"demonstrated on LLMBar, supporting trend on AlpacaEval (instruction-following), inconclusive on MT-Bench (task-specific).\\\"\\n\\n\\n新 benchmark 效应衰减是 median 档的核心预测。两个独立机制叠加造成衰减： (1) Counterfactual 质量下降——LLMBar 源文本是简洁的 instruction-following 对， formality rewriting 容易保内容；AlpacaEval 文本更长更多样，NLI pass rate 从 0.88 降到 0.83，丢弃更多样本 → 有效 n 减少；MT-Bench 包含数学/代码/推理等 domain 特异性强的文本，formality rewriting 更容易改变内容（把 \\\"Let's solve this step by step\\\" 改成正式版本可能改变推理链结构）→ NLI 降到 0.79。 (2) Formality 方差差异——LLMBar 的 instruction-following 文本天然有较大的 formality 方差（有的回答很 casual，有的很 formal），counterfactual contrast 大； MT-Bench 的技术性文本天然偏 formal，formality rewriting 的 contrast 小 → smaller effect size。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval 的 p=0.072 (trend) 符合 median 核心 假设 \\\"1 additional benchmark shows trend (p<0.10) but not clean significance\\\"。 Holm-Bonferroni 校正 (within GPT-4o: 0.006, 0.072, 0.214 → adjusted 0.018, 0.144, 0.214) 后只有 LLMBar survive。论文需诚实报告：\\\"effect replicates as trend on AlpacaEval but not MT-Bench\\\" 并讨论 benchmark 依赖性原因。\\n\"\n152\t  },\n153\t  {\n154\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n155\t    \"description\": \"对 9 个 judge × benchmark cells 系统计算 Likert ATE 和 binarized Likert sign test，与 pairwise win rate 对比。量化 C2 Likert Blindspot 的 replication rate 和 condition-dependence。\\n\",\n156\t    \"results\": {\n157\t      \"likert_ate\": {\n158\t        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n159\t          \"ate\": -0.102,\n160\t          \"se\": 0.149,\n161\t          \"p\": 0.332\n162\t        },\n163\t        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n164\t          \"ate\": -0.07,\n165\t          \"se\": 0.155,\n166\t          \"p\": 0.48\n167\t        },\n168\t        \"gpt4o_mtbench\": {\n169\t          \"ate\": -0.04,\n170\t          \"se\": 0.161,\n171\t          \"p\": 0.69\n172\t        },\n173\t        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n174\t          \"ate\": 0.03,\n175\t          \"se\": 0.158,\n176\t          \"p\": 0.71\n177\t        },\n178\t        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n179\t          \"ate\": -0.01,\n180\t          \"se\": 0.165,\n181\t          \"p\": 0.88\n182\t        },\n183\t        \"claude_mtbench\": {\n184\t          \"ate\": 0.02,\n185\t          \"se\": 0.17,\n186\t          \"p\": 0.82\n187\t        },\n188\t        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n189\t          \"ate\": -0.09,\n190\t          \"se\": 0.152,\n191\t          \"p\": 0.39\n192\t        },\n193\t        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n194\t          \"ate\": -0.06,\n195\t          \"se\": 0.16,\n196\t          \"p\": 0.53\n197\t        },\n198\t        \"gemini_mtbench\": {\n199\t          \"ate\": -0.03,\n200\t          \"se\": 0.168,\n201\t          \"p\": 0.76\n202\t        },\n203\t        \"any_significant\": false,\n204\t        \"note\": \"Likert ATE non-significant in all 9 cells; continuous Likert uniformly insensitive\"\n205\t      },\n206\t      \"binarized_likert\": {\n207\t        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n208\t          \"n_nontie\": 33,\n209\t          \"win_rate\": 0.606,\n210\t          \"p\": 0.296,\n211\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n212\t        },\n213\t        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n214\t          \"n_nontie\": 29,\n215\t          \"win_rate\": 0.586,\n216\t          \"p\": 0.108,\n217\t          \"status\": \"ambiguous\"\n218\t        },\n219\t        \"gpt4o_mtbench\": {\n220\t          \"n_nontie\": 26,\n221\t          \"win_rate\": 0.538,\n222\t          \"p\": 0.422,\n223\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n224\t        },\n225\t        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n226\t          \"n_nontie\": 27,\n227\t          \"win_rate\": 0.556,\n228\t          \"p\": 0.248,\n229\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n230\t        },\n231\t        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n232\t          \"n_nontie\": 23,\n233\t          \"win_rate\": 0.522,\n234\t          \"p\": 0.621,\n235\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n236\t        },\n237\t        \"claude_mtbench\": {\n238\t          \"n_nontie\": 21,\n239\t          \"win_rate\": 0.524,\n240\t          \"p\": 0.617,\n241\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n242\t        },\n243\t        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n244\t          \"n_nontie\": 30,\n245\t          \"win_rate\": 0.6,\n246\t          \"p\": 0.098,\n247\t          \"status\": \"ambiguous\"\n248\t        },\n249\t        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n250\t          \"n_nontie\": 25,\n251\t          \"win_rate\": 0.56,\n252\t          \"p\": 0.23,\n253\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n254\t        },\n255\t        \"gemini_mtbench\": {\n256\t          \"n_nontie\": 22,\n257\t          \"win_rate\": 0.5,\n258\t          \"p\": 1.0,\n259\t          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n260\t        }\n261\t      },\n262\t      \"binarized_likert_summary\": {\n263\t        \"non_significant_cells\": 7,\n264\t        \"ambiguous_cells_p005_012\": 2,\n265\t        \"significant_cells\": 0\n266\t      },\n267\t      \"c2_gap_analysis\": {\n268\t        \"cells_pairwise_sig_AND_likert_not\": 2,\n269\t        \"cells_pairwise_sig_AND_binarized_ambiguous\": 1,\n270\t        \"cells_pairwise_trend_AND_binarized_ambiguous\": 1,\n271\t        \"cells_both_non_sig\": 5,\n272\t        \"c2_clean_replication_rate\": 0.67,\n273\t        \"c2_with_ambiguous\": 0.5\n274\t      },\n275\t      \"measurement_amplification\": {\n276\t        \"mean_pairwise_effect_over_50pct\": 0.074,\n277\t        \"mean_binarized_likert_effect_over_50pct\": 0.044,\n278\t        \"amplification_ratio\": 1.68\n279\t      }\n280\t    },\n281\t    \"tables\": [\n282\t      {\n283\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Main results — Pairwise vs Likert vs Binarized Likert (9 cells)\",\n284\t        \"description\": \"Paper 的 main result table。9-cell grid (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)， each cell: Pairwise win_rate (p) | Likert ATE (p) | Binarized win_rate (p)。 Color coding: green p<0.05, yellow p<0.12, red p>0.12。 Final row: measurement amplification ratio per cell。\\n\"\n285\t      },\n286\t      {\n287\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: C2 gap categorization\",\n288\t        \"description\": \"Supplementary。Rows: 9 cells。Columns: pairwise_status (sig/marginal/null), binarized_status (non-sig/ambiguous), C2_gap (clean/ambiguous/no gap/NA)。 Summary: 2 clean, 1 ambiguous, 1 marginal-both, 5 both-null。\\n\"\n289\t      }\n290\t    ],\n291\t    \"figures\": [],\n292\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-003 是论文最重要的表格。Median 结果的叙事策略：(1) Lead with Likert ATE = 0/9 significant → continuous Likert 完全 blind，这是最强 version of C2；(2) Binarized Likert = 0/9 significant (2 ambiguous) vs Pairwise = 2/9 significant → gap exists but C2 需要 qualify 为 \\\"Likert Blindspot is a measurement efficiency gap, not absolute insensitivity\\\"；(3) Amplification ratio 1.68× provides quantitative hook for practitioners。§5.2 \\\"When Does the Blindspot Narrow?\\\" 分析 C2 gap 与 effect size 的关系——如果 pairwise effect 越大 gap 越大 (positive correlation)，说明 Likert 对所有 effect size 都 equally insensitive (stronger C2)；如果 gap 恒定， 说明只是 constant offset (weaker C2 but still useful)。\\n\\n\\nLikert ATE 全面不显著是 median 档的稳健预测——continuous Likert 的 within-pair 评分方差 (SE~0.15-0.17) 远大于 formality ATE (~0.05-0.10)，信噪比根本不足。 这是 structural 而非 power issue：即使 n→∞，如果 ATE 接近零（raw ATE 在 -0.10 到 +0.03 之间散布），continuous Likert 的 measurement noise 使得 effect 不 convergent。Binarized Likert 的 2 个 ambiguous cells 是 C2 的最大叙事张力： (a) Gemini×LLMBar binarized p=0.098 vs pairwise p=0.041——gap 存在但不大， reviewer 会质疑 \\\"is this just a power issue?\\\" 回答：effect size 差异（63.8% vs 60.0%）说明 pairwise 不仅 more powerful 而且 amplifies the signal—— amplification ratio 1.68× 是 structural advantage（pairwise 的 forced choice 消除了 Likert 的 tie/neutral responses 噪声）。(b) GPT-4o×AlpacaEval binarized p=0.108 vs pairwise p=0.072——两个都 marginal，gap 极小 → 这个 cell 不支持 C2。但在 5 个 null cells 中，pairwise 和 binarized Likert 都 null → C2 gap 只在 effect 存在时才有意义。整体：C2 replication rate 67%（2/3 significant pairwise cells 有 clean gap），但加入 ambiguous 考量降到 50%。论文需要 nuanced 表述：\\\"The Likert Blindspot is most pronounced when style bias is moderate (pairwise 60-70%); for strong effects, binarized Likert may approach detection; for null effects, no method detects.\\\"\\n\"\n293\t  },\n294\t  {\n295\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n296\t    \"description\": \"对所有 judge × benchmark 组合做 original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison， 量化 original preference confound。扩展 exp-014 的 GEE logistic decomposition 到所有条件。\\n\",\n297\t    \"results\": {\n298\t      \"original_preference_pairwise\": {\n299\t        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n300\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.585,\n301\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.052,\n302\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.82,\n303\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.052,\n304\t          \"note\": \"known from exp-014\"\n305\t        },\n306\t        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n307\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.545,\n308\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.232,\n309\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.38,\n310\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.245\n311\t        },\n312\t        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n313\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.625,\n314\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.026,\n315\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 2.18,\n316\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.03\n317\t        },\n318\t        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n319\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.57,\n320\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.105,\n321\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.58,\n322\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.112\n323\t        },\n324\t        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n325\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.53,\n326\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.396,\n327\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.22,\n328\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.41\n329\t        },\n330\t        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n331\t          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.58,\n332\t          \"original_pref_p\": 0.075,\n333\t          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.72,\n334\t          \"gee_original_p\": 0.082\n335\t        }\n336\t      },\n337\t      \"logistic_decomposition_extended\": {\n338\t        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n339\t          \"formality_OR\": 2.21,\n340\t          \"formality_p\": 0.01,\n341\t          \"original_OR\": 1.82,\n342\t          \"original_p\": 0.052,\n343\t          \"formality_exceeds_original\": true\n344\t        },\n345\t        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n346\t          \"formality_OR\": 1.95,\n347\t          \"formality_p\": 0.038,\n348\t          \"original_OR\": 2.18,\n349\t          \"original_p\": 0.03,\n350\t          \"formality_exceeds_original\": false,\n351\t          \"note\": \"CRITICAL: original preference OR exceeds formality OR for Gemini\"\n352\t        },\n353\t        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n354\t          \"formality_OR\": 1.52,\n355\t          \"formality_p\": 0.165,\n356\t          \"original_OR\": 1.38,\n357\t          \"original_p\": 0.245,\n358\t          \"formality_exceeds_original\": true,\n359\t          \"note\": \"neither significant — underpowered\"\n360\t        }\n361\t      },\n362\t      \"summary\": {\n363\t        \"judges_with_significant_original_pref\": 1,\n364\t        \"judges_with_marginal_original_pref\": 2,\n365\t        \"formality_still_dominates_for_gpt4o\": true,\n366\t        \"confound_problematic_for_gemini\": true\n367\t      }\n368\t    },\n369\t    \"tables\": [\n370\t      {\n371\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Original preference decomposition across judges\",\n372\t        \"description\": \"Rows: judge × benchmark (6 cells with data)。Columns: formality_OR (CI, p), original_pref_OR (CI, p), formality > original?, status。 GPT-4o×LLMBar highlighted as clean decomposition；Gemini×LLMBar flagged。\\n\"\n373\t      }\n374\t    ],\n375\t    \"figures\": [],\n376\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-005 使得 \\\"confound is negligible\\\" argument 不成立。但 \\\"confound is acknowledged and statistically controlled\\\" 在 GPT-4o 上仍然成立。对于 Gemini， 论文需要 paragraph: \\\"Gemini-Flash shows both formality preference and original preference; future work with larger n or improved double-rewrite protocol may achieve cleaner separation.\\\" 这实际上提供了有用的 method boundary：CSD 的 confound control 对某些 judge 更 effective（GPT-4o）比其他（Gemini）。 Practical implication for C4：recommend running original-preference control for each judge, and only report formality estimates where decomposition is clean。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference confound 在 median 档变得 judge-dependent，核心威胁来自 Gemini。机制：double-rewrite 虽设计为 style-preserving，仍不可避免引入 surface 变化（lexical micro-substitutions, sentence structure 微调）。不同 judge 对 这些 \\\"rewriting artifacts\\\" 的敏感度不同。Gemini-Flash 作为较小模型，对 surface form 变化更敏感 → double-rewrite 产生的微小质量损失被 Gemini 放大为显著 original preference (OR=2.18, p=0.026)。关键问题：Gemini×LLMBar 的 formality pairwise 显著 (p=0.041)，但 original preference 也显著 (p=0.026)，且 original OR (2.18) > formality OR (1.95) → 对 Gemini 来说，无法 cleanly separate formality bias from rewriting artifact。GPT-4o×LLMBar 保持 clean：formality OR (2.21) > original OR (1.82)，formality p=0.010 vs original p=0.052 → 可以 argue formality is the dominant effect。Claude 两者都不显著，无信息量。论文策略： primary claim 基于 GPT-4o×LLMBar (clean decomposition)；Gemini 的显著结果作为 \\\"replication with caveat\\\" — \\\"formality bias detected (p=0.041) but original preference cannot be ruled out as partial contributor (p=0.026).\\\" 这种 honesty 是 strength not weakness — reviewer 更信任 acknowledged confounds。\\n\"\n377\t  },\n378\t  {\n379\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n380\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar (最佳 cell) 从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。计算 pairwise、 binarized Likert、Likert ATE，直接检验 C2 是 structural blindspot 还是 power issue。Power analysis 量化 measurement efficiency gap。\\n\",\n381\t    \"results\": {\n382\t      \"pairwise\": {\n383\t        \"n_total\": 500,\n384\t        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n385\t        \"n_consistent\": 275,\n386\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.561,\n387\t        \"formal_wins\": 168,\n388\t        \"casual_wins\": 107,\n389\t        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.611,\n390\t        \"wilson_ci\": [\n391\t          0.552,\n392\t          0.667\n393\t        ],\n394\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.0004\n395\t      },\n396\t      \"binarized_likert\": {\n397\t        \"n_nli_ge90\": 435,\n398\t        \"n_nontie\": 163,\n399\t        \"formal_direction\": 94,\n400\t        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.577,\n401\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.063,\n402\t        \"wilson_ci\": [\n403\t          0.499,\n404\t          0.651\n405\t        ],\n406\t        \"note\": \"Approaches significance; NOT significant at alpha=0.05\"\n407\t      },\n408\t      \"likert_ate\": {\n409\t        \"n_primary\": 435,\n410\t        \"raw_ate\": -0.085,\n411\t        \"raw_se\": 0.065,\n412\t        \"raw_p\": 0.19,\n413\t        \"corrected_ate\": 0.095,\n414\t        \"corrected_se\": 0.047,\n415\t        \"corrected_p\": 0.043,\n416\t        \"note\": \"Raw ATE still wrong direction; corrected ATE barely significant\"\n417\t      },\n418\t      \"power_analysis\": {\n419\t        \"pairwise_detected_effect_cohens_h\": 0.222,\n420\t        \"binarized_likert_detected_effect_cohens_h\": 0.154,\n421\t        \"measurement_amplification_ratio\": 1.44,\n422\t        \"pairwise_power_at_n100\": 0.72,\n423\t        \"pairwise_power_at_n200\": 0.93,\n424\t        \"pairwise_power_at_n500\": 0.998,\n425\t        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n100\": 0.18,\n426\t        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n200\": 0.34,\n427\t        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n500\": 0.52,\n428\t        \"binarized_likert_n_for_80pct_power\": 680,\n429\t        \"likert_ate_power_at_n100\": 0.09,\n430\t        \"likert_ate_power_at_n500\": 0.31,\n431\t        \"likert_ate_n_for_80pct_power\": 1200\n432\t      },\n433\t      \"regression_to_mean\": {\n434\t        \"n100_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.691,\n435\t        \"n500_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.611,\n436\t        \"regression_magnitude\": 0.08,\n437\t        \"note\": \"8pp regression consistent with sampling variance at n=55 consistent pairs\"\n438\t      }\n439\t    },\n440\t    \"tables\": [\n441\t      {\n442\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Scaled replication — measurement comparison at n=500\",\n443\t        \"description\": \"3 rows (Pairwise, Binarized Likert, Likert ATE) × columns: n_effective, effect_estimate, 95% CI, p-value, Cohen's h, power_at_n100, power_at_n500, n_for_80pct_power。Clearly shows efficiency hierarchy。\\n\"\n444\t      },\n445\t      {\n446\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: n=100 vs n=500 comparison\",\n447\t        \"description\": \"Side-by-side: all metrics at two sample sizes。Regression to mean quantified and contextualized。\\n\"\n448\t      }\n449\t    ],\n450\t    \"figures\": [],\n451\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 redefines C2 from \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" to \\\"Likert Efficiency Gap.\\\" Binarized Likert p=0.063 at n=500 means the effect is detectable in principle — given enough data. But the practical gap (pairwise needs n~110, binarized Likert needs n~680) is the real contribution. For practitioners: \\\"If you suspect style bias, pairwise comparison with n=100 is sufficient; Likert scoring would need n≥700 for the same statistical power.\\\" Title 可能需要从 \\\"Blindspot\\\" 软化为 \\\"Blind Spot\\\" 或保留但 在 abstract 中 qualify。Power analysis table 是最 reviewer-friendly 的结果之一—— 直接 actionable guidance。Win rate 回归到 61.1% 需要 honestly report，不要 buried in supplement。\\n\\n\\nn=500 的三个关键结果及其 rationale： (1) Pairwise win rate 从 69.1% 回归到 61.1%。n=100 的 69.1% 来自仅 55 个 consistent pairs → 采样方差大，Wilson CI [56.0%, 79.7%]。n=500 的 275 个 consistent pairs 给出更精确的 true effect estimate ~61%。8pp 回归幅度在 n=55 的 CI 范围内，统计上完全预期。效应仍高度显著 (p=0.0004)。 (2) Binarized Likert p=0.063：在 n=500 下 approaching 但 NOT crossing 0.05 线。 这是 median 档的精妙预测——如果 binarized Likert 真的 significant，C2 从 \\\"blindspot\\\" 变成 \\\"efficiency gap\\\"，论文核心受损；如果完全 null，C2 过于强势 反而可疑。p=0.063 恰好在模糊地带：它说明 binarized Likert 不是完全 blind（有 trending signal），但需要远超 pairwise 的样本量才能 detect → \\\"efficiency gap\\\" framing 是准确的。关键：binarized Likert n_nontie=163 (Likert 评分相同的 pair 被丢弃 → 信息损失)，effective n 仅 pairwise 的 59%，这是 structural 不是 power。 (3) Likert ATE raw p=0.19 仍不显著且方向错误 → continuous Likert 在 n=500 下 仍然 blind。Corrected ATE (accounting for rewrite bias) p=0.043 barely significant，但 \\\"corrected\\\" 需要知道 rewrite bias → 不是 post-hoc 可用的检测 工具。这进一步支持 \\\"Likert cannot serve as style bias detector without correction.\\\" Power analysis 的实用价值：pairwise 在 n=100 就有 72% power (接近 80%)， binarized Likert 需要 n=680 for 80% power → 6.8× 样本量差距。这是论文的 quantitative C2 claim：\\\"pairwise comparison is ~7× more sample-efficient than binarized Likert for detecting style bias at the observed effect size.\\\"\\n\"\n452\t  },\n453\t  {\n454\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n455\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上 重复 formality counterfactual generation + pairwise pipeline。排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n456\t    \"results\": {\n457\t      \"counterfactual_quality\": {\n458\t        \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.81,\n459\t        \"bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.75,\n460\t        \"both_pass_rate\": 0.73,\n461\t        \"nli_mean\": 0.869,\n462\t        \"bertscore_mean\": 0.905,\n463\t        \"nli_std\": 0.298,\n464\t        \"comparison_vs_qwen\": {\n465\t          \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n466\t          \"qwen_both_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n467\t          \"llama_nli_delta\": -0.07,\n468\t          \"note\": \"Llama slightly worse at style transfer precision\"\n469\t        }\n470\t      },\n471\t      \"pairwise_results\": {\n472\t        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 95,\n473\t        \"n_consistent\": 48,\n474\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.505,\n475\t        \"formal_wins\": 30,\n476\t        \"casual_wins\": 18,\n477\t        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.625,\n478\t        \"wilson_ci\": [\n479\t          0.48,\n480\t          0.749\n481\t        ],\n482\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.042,\n483\t        \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.72,\n484\t        \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n485\t      },\n486\t      \"comparison_with_qwen\": {\n487\t        \"qwen_win_rate\": 0.691,\n488\t        \"llama_win_rate\": 0.625,\n489\t        \"difference\": 0.066,\n490\t        \"difference_p\": 0.43,\n491\t        \"direction_consistent\": true,\n492\t        \"sign_consistent\": true,\n493\t        \"magnitude_within_qwen_ci\": true,\n494\t        \"note\": \"6.6pp difference not significant; both within Qwen's [56.0%, 79.7%] CI\"\n495\t      }\n496\t    },\n497\t    \"tables\": [\n498\t      {\n499\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: Rewriter robustness check\",\n500\t        \"description\": \"2 rows (Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B) × columns: NLI_pass_rate, BERTScore_pass_rate, n_consistent, formal_win_rate (CI, p), direction_asymmetry。Footnote: chi-squared test for win_rate difference p=0.43。\\n\"\n501\t      }\n502\t    ],\n503\t    \"figures\": [],\n504\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 是 reviewer 几乎必问的 robustness check。Median 结果提供 clean answer： \\\"direction robust, magnitude varies.\\\" 论文中 1-2 段：acknowledge rewriter dependence, recommend reporting rewriter choice as method parameter。如果 reviewer 要求第三个 rewriter，可以 argue \\\"two independent rewriters with consistent direction provides reasonable evidence against rewriter-specific artifacts; exhaustive rewriter comparison is beyond scope.\\\" Cost: 8 GPU hours for Llama-70B generation。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.1-70B 的 style transfer 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B 是预期中的——Qwen3-32B 在 instruction following 和 controlled generation 任务上经过更充分的训练。 NLI pass rate 0.81 vs 0.88 的差距来自 Llama 在 style rewriting 时更容易引入 minor content modifications (添加 qualifiers, 重组 argument structure)。 Pairwise win rate 衰减到 62.5% (vs Qwen 的 69.1%) 有两个可能原因：(a) lower NLI pass rate → 更多边缘质量的 counterfactual 被保留 (NLI 0.81-0.90 的样本 content preservation 较差) → diluting the signal；(b) Llama 的 style transfer 不够 \\\"extreme\\\" — formal counterfactual 不够 formal，contrast 较小。但方向完全 一致 (formal wins)，p=0.042 显著，6.6pp 差异在 Qwen 的 CI 内 (p_diff=0.43)。 这足以 rule out \\\"Qwen-specific artifact\\\" 但引入 nuance: \\\"rewriter choice moderates effect magnitude (~7pp) even when direction is robust.\\\" 对方法论的 implication：CSD 应报告 rewriter choice 并建议用多个 rewriter 取均值或报告 range。论文一段话足矣。\\n\"\n505\t  },\n506\t  {\n507\t    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation\",\n508\t    \"description\": \"100 counterfactual pairs 的 human annotation (content preservation judgment)。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)、precision、recall。使用 LLM-as-annotator + human spot check。\\n\",\n509\t    \"results\": {\n510\t      \"annotation_summary\": {\n511\t        \"n_annotated\": 100,\n512\t        \"human_pass\": 95,\n513\t        \"human_fail\": 5,\n514\t        \"nli_pass\": 88,\n515\t        \"nli_fail\": 12\n516\t      },\n517\t      \"confusion_matrix\": {\n518\t        \"tp\": 87,\n519\t        \"fp\": 1,\n520\t        \"fn\": 8,\n521\t        \"tn\": 4\n522\t      },\n523\t      \"agreement_metrics\": {\n524\t        \"raw_agreement\": 0.91,\n525\t        \"cohens_kappa\": 0.43,\n526\t        \"pabak\": 0.82,\n527\t        \"prevalence_index\": 0.83\n528\t      },\n529\t      \"precision_recall\": {\n530\t        \"nli_precision\": 0.989,\n531\t        \"nli_recall\": 0.916,\n532\t        \"nli_f1\": 0.951,\n533\t        \"nli_specificity\": 0.8\n534\t      },\n535\t      \"false_negative_analysis\": {\n536\t        \"n_false_negatives\": 8,\n537\t        \"categories\": {\n538\t          \"paraphrase_level_changes\": 5,\n539\t          \"minor_lexical_substitution\": 2,\n540\t          \"borderline_content_addition\": 1\n541\t        },\n542\t        \"mean_nli_score_of_fn\": 0.78,\n543\t        \"note\": \"FNs cluster at NLI 0.75-0.88 — NLI is strict on borderline cases\"\n544\t      },\n545\t      \"false_positive_analysis\": {\n546\t        \"n_false_positives\": 1,\n547\t        \"category\": \"subtle_factual_drift\",\n548\t        \"nli_score\": 0.93,\n549\t        \"note\": \"NLI missed minor factual change that human caught; extremely rare\"\n550\t      }\n551\t    },\n552\t    \"tables\": [\n553\t      {\n554\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: Human validation confusion matrix\",\n555\t        \"description\": \"2×2 matrix with margins。Below: kappa=0.43, PABAK=0.82, prevalence index=0.83, precision=98.9%, recall=91.6%。Footnote explaining PABAK and why it's more appropriate than raw kappa at 95% base rate。\\n\"\n556\t      },\n557\t      {\n558\t        \"name\": \"Table S5: False negative error analysis\",\n559\t        \"description\": \"8 FN examples。Columns: sample_id, NLI_score, change_type (paraphrase/ lexical/borderline), human_judgment_confidence, example_excerpt。 Shows NLI is strict-but-reasonable on borderline cases。\\n\"\n560\t      }\n561\t    ],\n562\t    \"figures\": [],\n563\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-013 需要最 careful 的 presentation。论文策略：(1) §3.2 先 report precision 98.9% 和 \\\"conservative gate\\\" framing（\\\"our NLI gate prioritizes precision over recall — passed pairs are near-certainly content-preserving\\\"）；(2) Full metrics including kappa 放在 §3.2 的后半段或 Appendix A，accompanied by class imbalance discussion；(3) PABAK=0.82 作为 robustness metric；(4) 3 annotated examples in Appendix (1 TP, 1 TN, 1 FN showing NLI's conservative behavior)。如果 reviewer 仍 push back on kappa<0.60，rebuttal 的核心论点：\\\"Cohen's kappa is known to underestimate agreement under extreme class imbalance (Feinstein & Cicchetti 1990, Prevalence Index = 0.83); PABAK corrects for this (0.82, excellent agreement). More importantly, our experimental design requires that passed pairs preserve content (precision = 98.9%), not that all content-preserving pairs pass (recall). The 8.4% recall loss reduces effective sample size but does not compromise validity.\\\"\\n\\nKappa=0.43 看似平庸但实际由 class imbalance 驱动而非真正 disagreement。 机制：100 pairs 中 95 个 human 判 \\\"pass\\\"、5 个 \\\"fail\\\"。在 base rate 95% 的 情况下，即使完美 agreement 在 majority class、只有少量 minority class 分歧， kappa 也会被严重压低。具体：8 个 false negative (NLI reject human accept)  来自 NLI 对 borderline 变化的过严判断——NLI entailment model 对 paraphrase 级 别的词汇替换 (synonyms, sentence restructuring) 给出 0.75-0.88 分，低于 0.90 threshold，但 human annotator 认为 content preserved。这说明 NLI gate 是 \\\"conservative\\\" 而非 \\\"wrong\\\"——它丢弃了 human 认为 OK 的 borderline cases， 损失 recall (8/95=8.4%) 但不损失 precision (只有 1/88=1.1% false positive)。 对论文的影响：NLI gate 通过的 counterfactual 几乎确定 content preserved (precision 98.9%)，这才是实验设计需要的保证。recall 损失只影响 effective n (sample size reduction ~12%)，不影响 validity。PABAK=0.82 (excellent agreement) 在 class imbalance 校正后远高于 raw kappa。但 reviewer 可能只看 kappa headline → 需要 proactive defense。\\n\"\n564\t  }\n565\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70b3cec-1f5f-4d61-b1ce-ec47e4d4a476","uuid":"ab06c249-947d-464d-a73e-648a2b382ecc","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:29:38.918Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T010111/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 LLMBar formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactuals，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge， position-controlled dual-direction protocol。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claude_sonnet\": {\n        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 96,\n        \"n_consistent\": 50,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.521,\n        \"formal_wins\": 29,\n        \"casual_wins\": 21,\n        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.58,\n        \"wilson_ci\": [\n          0.442,\n          0.706\n        ],\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.161,\n        \"position_bias_overall_A\": 0.52,\n        \"direction_formal_to_casual\": {\n          \"n\": 30,\n          \"formal_wins\": 19,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.633,\n          \"p\": 0.1\n        },\n        \"direction_casual_to_formal\": {\n          \"n\": 20,\n          \"formal_wins\": 10,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.5,\n          \"p\": 1.0\n        }\n      },\n      \"gemini_20_flash\": {\n        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 97,\n        \"n_consistent\": 47,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.485,\n        \"formal_wins\": 30,\n        \"casual_wins\": 17,\n        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.638,\n        \"wilson_ci\": [\n          0.495,\n          0.761\n        ],\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.041,\n        \"position_bias_overall_A\": 0.56,\n        \"direction_formal_to_casual\": {\n          \"n\": 28,\n          \"formal_wins\": 22,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.786,\n          \"p\": 0.002\n        },\n        \"direction_casual_to_formal\": {\n          \"n\": 19,\n          \"formal_wins\": 8,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.421,\n          \"p\": 0.648\n        }\n      },\n      \"cross_judge_summary\": {\n        \"judges_significant_p005\": 1,\n        \"judges_marginal_p005_015\": 1,\n        \"judges_null\": 0,\n        \"gpt4o_reference_win_rate\": 0.691,\n        \"best_non_gpt4o_win_rate\": 0.638,\n        \"win_rate_attenuation_vs_gpt4o\": 0.053\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2a: Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)\",\n        \"description\": \"3 rows (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) × columns: n_consistent, consistency_rate, formal_win_rate, 95% Wilson CI, sign_test_p, formal→casual_win_rate, casual→formal_win_rate, position_bias. GPT-4o 行 bolded (primary)，Gemini 行 starred (significant replication)。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C1 表述降级为 \\\"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006), replicated on Gemini-Flash (p=0.041), not detected on Claude-Sonnet (p=0.161, possibly underpowered).\\\" Claude 的 null 不能确定是 \\\"无 bias\\\" 还是 \\\"power 不足\\\"——需在论文中讨论 power (at n=50 consistent, MDE≈0.18 for pairwise win_rate → 58% 在 detection boundary 上)。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异增加了 §5 Discussion 的复杂度但也增加 了 depth——\\\"why does asymmetry vary?\\\" 可以链接到 judge 的 RLHF 训练差异。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预测 style bias 是真实效应但跨 judge 有系统性衰减。Gemini-Flash 显著 (p=0.041) 的机制：Flash 模型的 RLHF 投入较少 debiasing → 保留更强的 surface style preference；但效应量从 GPT-4o 的 69.1% 衰减到 63.8%，因为 Gemini 的 pairwise 一致性率较低 (48.5% vs GPT-4o 56.1%)，引入更多噪声对。Claude-Sonnet 不显著 (p=0.161) 的机制：Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程更保守，Constitutional AI 训练 可能部分抑制 surface style preference；加上 Claude 的 consistency_rate 只有 52.1%，有效 n 从 50 对中仅 29 个 formal wins → 检验力不足。Direction asymmetry 的 judge 间差异是 median 档的关键特征：Gemini 与 GPT-4o 类似，formal→casual 方向强 (78.6%)、casual→formal 方向 null (42.1%)；但 Claude 的不对称性更弱 (63.3% vs 50.0%)，且 casual→formal 方向完全平坦。这使得 \\\"formal→casual 方向 驱动效应\\\" 的叙事不能跨 judge 推广——只能说 \\\"direction asymmetry is judge-dependent, consistently observed for GPT-4o and Gemini but not Claude.\\\" 一致性率的 judge 间差异本身值得报告：它反映不同 judge 的 position sensitivity， 不是方法的失败而是 judge 特性的测量。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上新生成 formality counterfactuals，GPT-4o + Claude-Sonnet + Gemini-Flash 作为 judge 运行完整 CSD pairwise pipeline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"counterfactual_generation\": {\n        \"alpacaeval_nli_pass_rate\": 0.83,\n        \"alpacaeval_bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n        \"alpacaeval_both_pass_rate\": 0.78,\n        \"mtbench_nli_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n        \"mtbench_bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.74,\n        \"mtbench_both_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n        \"note\": \"NLI pass rate drops vs LLMBar (0.88) due to more diverse/technical source texts\"\n      },\n      \"alpacaeval\": {\n        \"gpt4o\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 51,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.608,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.072,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.7,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"claude_sonnet\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 44,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.348,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.58,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"gemini_flash\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 42,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.595,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.109,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.68,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.48\n        }\n      },\n      \"mt_bench\": {\n        \"gpt4o\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 46,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.565,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.214,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.62,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"claude_sonnet\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 40,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.525,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.557,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.54,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"gemini_flash\": {\n          \"n_consistent\": 39,\n          \"formal_win_rate\": 0.538,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.396,\n          \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.6,\n          \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.47\n        }\n      },\n      \"cross_benchmark_summary\": {\n        \"cells_significant_p005\": 0,\n        \"cells_trend_p005_010\": 1,\n        \"cells_trend_p010_015\": 1,\n        \"cells_null\": 4,\n        \"benchmark_ordering\": \"LLMBar >> AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\",\n        \"nli_pass_rate_ordering\": \"LLMBar (0.88) > AlpacaEval (0.83) > MT-Bench (0.79)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2b: Full 3×3 judge × benchmark pairwise results\",\n        \"description\": \"9-cell grid。Rows: LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench。Columns grouped by judge， each showing formal_win_rate (p-value)。p<0.05 bolded，p<0.10 italicized。 Only 2 bold cells (GPT-4o×LLMBar, Gemini×LLMBar)，2 italic (GPT-4o×AlpacaEval, Gemini×AlpacaEval)。Additional column: NLI pass rate per benchmark。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 确认 formality bias 不是 LLMBar artifact——AlpacaEval 上 GPT-4o 和 Gemini 都显示 trend (p<0.12)——但 effect magnitude 确实 benchmark-dependent。 论文需要 §5.1 \\\"Benchmark Dependence\\\" 讨论三个 benchmark 的差异，linking to counterfactual quality (NLI pass rate) 和 formality 方差。MT-Bench 的 null 结果 本身有 method boundary 意义：when source texts are domain-specific/technical， formality rewriting 更可能失败 NLI gate → CSD 方法自动 degrades gracefully。 Claim 从 \\\"across benchmarks\\\" 降级为 \\\"demonstrated on LLMBar, supporting trend on AlpacaEval (instruction-following), inconclusive on MT-Bench (task-specific).\\\"\\n\\n\\n新 benchmark 效应衰减是 median 档的核心预测。两个独立机制叠加造成衰减： (1) Counterfactual 质量下降——LLMBar 源文本是简洁的 instruction-following 对， formality rewriting 容易保内容；AlpacaEval 文本更长更多样，NLI pass rate 从 0.88 降到 0.83，丢弃更多样本 → 有效 n 减少；MT-Bench 包含数学/代码/推理等 domain 特异性强的文本，formality rewriting 更容易改变内容（把 \\\"Let's solve this step by step\\\" 改成正式版本可能改变推理链结构）→ NLI 降到 0.79。 (2) Formality 方差差异——LLMBar 的 instruction-following 文本天然有较大的 formality 方差（有的回答很 casual，有的很 formal），counterfactual contrast 大； MT-Bench 的技术性文本天然偏 formal，formality rewriting 的 contrast 小 → smaller effect size。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval 的 p=0.072 (trend) 符合 median 核心 假设 \\\"1 additional benchmark shows trend (p<0.10) but not clean significance\\\"。 Holm-Bonferroni 校正 (within GPT-4o: 0.006, 0.072, 0.214 → adjusted 0.018, 0.144, 0.214) 后只有 LLMBar survive。论文需诚实报告：\\\"effect replicates as trend on AlpacaEval but not MT-Bench\\\" 并讨论 benchmark 依赖性原因。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对 9 个 judge × benchmark cells 系统计算 Likert ATE 和 binarized Likert sign test，与 pairwise win rate 对比。量化 C2 Likert Blindspot 的 replication rate 和 condition-dependence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"likert_ate\": {\n        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.102,\n          \"se\": 0.149,\n          \"p\": 0.332\n        },\n        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.07,\n          \"se\": 0.155,\n          \"p\": 0.48\n        },\n        \"gpt4o_mtbench\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.04,\n          \"se\": 0.161,\n          \"p\": 0.69\n        },\n        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n          \"ate\": 0.03,\n          \"se\": 0.158,\n          \"p\": 0.71\n        },\n        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.01,\n          \"se\": 0.165,\n          \"p\": 0.88\n        },\n        \"claude_mtbench\": {\n          \"ate\": 0.02,\n          \"se\": 0.17,\n          \"p\": 0.82\n        },\n        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.09,\n          \"se\": 0.152,\n          \"p\": 0.39\n        },\n        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.06,\n          \"se\": 0.16,\n          \"p\": 0.53\n        },\n        \"gemini_mtbench\": {\n          \"ate\": -0.03,\n          \"se\": 0.168,\n          \"p\": 0.76\n        },\n        \"any_significant\": false,\n        \"note\": \"Likert ATE non-significant in all 9 cells; continuous Likert uniformly insensitive\"\n      },\n      \"binarized_likert\": {\n        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 33,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.606,\n          \"p\": 0.296,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 29,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.586,\n          \"p\": 0.108,\n          \"status\": \"ambiguous\"\n        },\n        \"gpt4o_mtbench\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 26,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.538,\n          \"p\": 0.422,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 27,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.556,\n          \"p\": 0.248,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 23,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.522,\n          \"p\": 0.621,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"claude_mtbench\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 21,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.524,\n          \"p\": 0.617,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 30,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.6,\n          \"p\": 0.098,\n          \"status\": \"ambiguous\"\n        },\n        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 25,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.56,\n          \"p\": 0.23,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        },\n        \"gemini_mtbench\": {\n          \"n_nontie\": 22,\n          \"win_rate\": 0.5,\n          \"p\": 1.0,\n          \"status\": \"non-significant\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"binarized_likert_summary\": {\n        \"non_significant_cells\": 7,\n        \"ambiguous_cells_p005_012\": 2,\n        \"significant_cells\": 0\n      },\n      \"c2_gap_analysis\": {\n        \"cells_pairwise_sig_AND_likert_not\": 2,\n        \"cells_pairwise_sig_AND_binarized_ambiguous\": 1,\n        \"cells_pairwise_trend_AND_binarized_ambiguous\": 1,\n        \"cells_both_non_sig\": 5,\n        \"c2_clean_replication_rate\": 0.67,\n        \"c2_with_ambiguous\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"measurement_amplification\": {\n        \"mean_pairwise_effect_over_50pct\": 0.074,\n        \"mean_binarized_likert_effect_over_50pct\": 0.044,\n        \"amplification_ratio\": 1.68\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Main results — Pairwise vs Likert vs Binarized Likert (9 cells)\",\n        \"description\": \"Paper 的 main result table。9-cell grid (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)， each cell: Pairwise win_rate (p) | Likert ATE (p) | Binarized win_rate (p)。 Color coding: green p<0.05, yellow p<0.12, red p>0.12。 Final row: measurement amplification ratio per cell。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: C2 gap categorization\",\n        \"description\": \"Supplementary。Rows: 9 cells。Columns: pairwise_status (sig/marginal/null), binarized_status (non-sig/ambiguous), C2_gap (clean/ambiguous/no gap/NA)。 Summary: 2 clean, 1 ambiguous, 1 marginal-both, 5 both-null。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-003 是论文最重要的表格。Median 结果的叙事策略：(1) Lead with Likert ATE = 0/9 significant → continuous Likert 完全 blind，这是最强 version of C2；(2) Binarized Likert = 0/9 significant (2 ambiguous) vs Pairwise = 2/9 significant → gap exists but C2 需要 qualify 为 \\\"Likert Blindspot is a measurement efficiency gap, not absolute insensitivity\\\"；(3) Amplification ratio 1.68× provides quantitative hook for practitioners。§5.2 \\\"When Does the Blindspot Narrow?\\\" 分析 C2 gap 与 effect size 的关系——如果 pairwise effect 越大 gap 越大 (positive correlation)，说明 Likert 对所有 effect size 都 equally insensitive (stronger C2)；如果 gap 恒定， 说明只是 constant offset (weaker C2 but still useful)。\\n\\n\\nLikert ATE 全面不显著是 median 档的稳健预测——continuous Likert 的 within-pair 评分方差 (SE~0.15-0.17) 远大于 formality ATE (~0.05-0.10)，信噪比根本不足。 这是 structural 而非 power issue：即使 n→∞，如果 ATE 接近零（raw ATE 在 -0.10 到 +0.03 之间散布），continuous Likert 的 measurement noise 使得 effect 不 convergent。Binarized Likert 的 2 个 ambiguous cells 是 C2 的最大叙事张力： (a) Gemini×LLMBar binarized p=0.098 vs pairwise p=0.041——gap 存在但不大， reviewer 会质疑 \\\"is this just a power issue?\\\" 回答：effect size 差异（63.8% vs 60.0%）说明 pairwise 不仅 more powerful 而且 amplifies the signal—— amplification ratio 1.68× 是 structural advantage（pairwise 的 forced choice 消除了 Likert 的 tie/neutral responses 噪声）。(b) GPT-4o×AlpacaEval binarized p=0.108 vs pairwise p=0.072——两个都 marginal，gap 极小 → 这个 cell 不支持 C2。但在 5 个 null cells 中，pairwise 和 binarized Likert 都 null → C2 gap 只在 effect 存在时才有意义。整体：C2 replication rate 67%（2/3 significant pairwise cells 有 clean gap），但加入 ambiguous 考量降到 50%。论文需要 nuanced 表述：\\\"The Likert Blindspot is most pronounced when style bias is moderate (pairwise 60-70%); for strong effects, binarized Likert may approach detection; for null effects, no method detects.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"对所有 judge × benchmark 组合做 original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison， 量化 original preference confound。扩展 exp-014 的 GEE logistic decomposition 到所有条件。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"original_preference_pairwise\": {\n        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.585,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.052,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.82,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.052,\n          \"note\": \"known from exp-014\"\n        },\n        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.545,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.232,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.38,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.245\n        },\n        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.625,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.026,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 2.18,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.03\n        },\n        \"gpt4o_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.57,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.105,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.58,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.112\n        },\n        \"claude_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.53,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.396,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.22,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.41\n        },\n        \"gemini_alpacaeval\": {\n          \"original_pref_win_rate\": 0.58,\n          \"original_pref_p\": 0.075,\n          \"gee_original_OR\": 1.72,\n          \"gee_original_p\": 0.082\n        }\n      },\n      \"logistic_decomposition_extended\": {\n        \"gpt4o_llmbar\": {\n          \"formality_OR\": 2.21,\n          \"formality_p\": 0.01,\n          \"original_OR\": 1.82,\n          \"original_p\": 0.052,\n          \"formality_exceeds_original\": true\n        },\n        \"gemini_llmbar\": {\n          \"formality_OR\": 1.95,\n          \"formality_p\": 0.038,\n          \"original_OR\": 2.18,\n          \"original_p\": 0.03,\n          \"formality_exceeds_original\": false,\n          \"note\": \"CRITICAL: original preference OR exceeds formality OR for Gemini\"\n        },\n        \"claude_llmbar\": {\n          \"formality_OR\": 1.52,\n          \"formality_p\": 0.165,\n          \"original_OR\": 1.38,\n          \"original_p\": 0.245,\n          \"formality_exceeds_original\": true,\n          \"note\": \"neither significant — underpowered\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"summary\": {\n        \"judges_with_significant_original_pref\": 1,\n        \"judges_with_marginal_original_pref\": 2,\n        \"formality_still_dominates_for_gpt4o\": true,\n        \"confound_problematic_for_gemini\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Original preference decomposition across judges\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: judge × benchmark (6 cells with data)。Columns: formality_OR (CI, p), original_pref_OR (CI, p), formality > original?, status。 GPT-4o×LLMBar highlighted as clean decomposition；Gemini×LLMBar flagged。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-005 使得 \\\"confound is negligible\\\" argument 不成立。但 \\\"confound is acknowledged and statistically controlled\\\" 在 GPT-4o 上仍然成立。对于 Gemini， 论文需要 paragraph: \\\"Gemini-Flash shows both formality preference and original preference; future work with larger n or improved double-rewrite protocol may achieve cleaner separation.\\\" 这实际上提供了有用的 method boundary：CSD 的 confound control 对某些 judge 更 effective（GPT-4o）比其他（Gemini）。 Practical implication for C4：recommend running original-preference control for each judge, and only report formality estimates where decomposition is clean。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference confound 在 median 档变得 judge-dependent，核心威胁来自 Gemini。机制：double-rewrite 虽设计为 style-preserving，仍不可避免引入 surface 变化（lexical micro-substitutions, sentence structure 微调）。不同 judge 对 这些 \\\"rewriting artifacts\\\" 的敏感度不同。Gemini-Flash 作为较小模型，对 surface form 变化更敏感 → double-rewrite 产生的微小质量损失被 Gemini 放大为显著 original preference (OR=2.18, p=0.026)。关键问题：Gemini×LLMBar 的 formality pairwise 显著 (p=0.041)，但 original preference 也显著 (p=0.026)，且 original OR (2.18) > formality OR (1.95) → 对 Gemini 来说，无法 cleanly separate formality bias from rewriting artifact。GPT-4o×LLMBar 保持 clean：formality OR (2.21) > original OR (1.82)，formality p=0.010 vs original p=0.052 → 可以 argue formality is the dominant effect。Claude 两者都不显著，无信息量。论文策略： primary claim 基于 GPT-4o×LLMBar (clean decomposition)；Gemini 的显著结果作为 \\\"replication with caveat\\\" — \\\"formality bias detected (p=0.041) but original preference cannot be ruled out as partial contributor (p=0.026).\\\" 这种 honesty 是 strength not weakness — reviewer 更信任 acknowledged confounds。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar (最佳 cell) 从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。计算 pairwise、 binarized Likert、Likert ATE，直接检验 C2 是 structural blindspot 还是 power issue。Power analysis 量化 measurement efficiency gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pairwise\": {\n        \"n_total\": 500,\n        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n        \"n_consistent\": 275,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.561,\n        \"formal_wins\": 168,\n        \"casual_wins\": 107,\n        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.611,\n        \"wilson_ci\": [\n          0.552,\n          0.667\n        ],\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.0004\n      },\n      \"binarized_likert\": {\n        \"n_nli_ge90\": 435,\n        \"n_nontie\": 163,\n        \"formal_direction\": 94,\n        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.577,\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.063,\n        \"wilson_ci\": [\n          0.499,\n          0.651\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Approaches significance; NOT significant at alpha=0.05\"\n      },\n      \"likert_ate\": {\n        \"n_primary\": 435,\n        \"raw_ate\": -0.085,\n        \"raw_se\": 0.065,\n        \"raw_p\": 0.19,\n        \"corrected_ate\": 0.095,\n        \"corrected_se\": 0.047,\n        \"corrected_p\": 0.043,\n        \"note\": \"Raw ATE still wrong direction; corrected ATE barely significant\"\n      },\n      \"power_analysis\": {\n        \"pairwise_detected_effect_cohens_h\": 0.222,\n        \"binarized_likert_detected_effect_cohens_h\": 0.154,\n        \"measurement_amplification_ratio\": 1.44,\n        \"pairwise_power_at_n100\": 0.72,\n        \"pairwise_power_at_n200\": 0.93,\n        \"pairwise_power_at_n500\": 0.998,\n        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n100\": 0.18,\n        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n200\": 0.34,\n        \"binarized_likert_power_at_n500\": 0.52,\n        \"binarized_likert_n_for_80pct_power\": 680,\n        \"likert_ate_power_at_n100\": 0.09,\n        \"likert_ate_power_at_n500\": 0.31,\n        \"likert_ate_n_for_80pct_power\": 1200\n      },\n      \"regression_to_mean\": {\n        \"n100_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.691,\n        \"n500_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.611,\n        \"regression_magnitude\": 0.08,\n        \"note\": \"8pp regression consistent with sampling variance at n=55 consistent pairs\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Scaled replication — measurement comparison at n=500\",\n        \"description\": \"3 rows (Pairwise, Binarized Likert, Likert ATE) × columns: n_effective, effect_estimate, 95% CI, p-value, Cohen's h, power_at_n100, power_at_n500, n_for_80pct_power。Clearly shows efficiency hierarchy。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: n=100 vs n=500 comparison\",\n        \"description\": \"Side-by-side: all metrics at two sample sizes。Regression to mean quantified and contextualized。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 redefines C2 from \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" to \\\"Likert Efficiency Gap.\\\" Binarized Likert p=0.063 at n=500 means the effect is detectable in principle — given enough data. But the practical gap (pairwise needs n~110, binarized Likert needs n~680) is the real contribution. For practitioners: \\\"If you suspect style bias, pairwise comparison with n=100 is sufficient; Likert scoring would need n≥700 for the same statistical power.\\\" Title 可能需要从 \\\"Blindspot\\\" 软化为 \\\"Blind Spot\\\" 或保留但 在 abstract 中 qualify。Power analysis table 是最 reviewer-friendly 的结果之一—— 直接 actionable guidance。Win rate 回归到 61.1% 需要 honestly report，不要 buried in supplement。\\n\\n\\nn=500 的三个关键结果及其 rationale： (1) Pairwise win rate 从 69.1% 回归到 61.1%。n=100 的 69.1% 来自仅 55 个 consistent pairs → 采样方差大，Wilson CI [56.0%, 79.7%]。n=500 的 275 个 consistent pairs 给出更精确的 true effect estimate ~61%。8pp 回归幅度在 n=55 的 CI 范围内，统计上完全预期。效应仍高度显著 (p=0.0004)。 (2) Binarized Likert p=0.063：在 n=500 下 approaching 但 NOT crossing 0.05 线。 这是 median 档的精妙预测——如果 binarized Likert 真的 significant，C2 从 \\\"blindspot\\\" 变成 \\\"efficiency gap\\\"，论文核心受损；如果完全 null，C2 过于强势 反而可疑。p=0.063 恰好在模糊地带：它说明 binarized Likert 不是完全 blind（有 trending signal），但需要远超 pairwise 的样本量才能 detect → \\\"efficiency gap\\\" framing 是准确的。关键：binarized Likert n_nontie=163 (Likert 评分相同的 pair 被丢弃 → 信息损失)，effective n 仅 pairwise 的 59%，这是 structural 不是 power。 (3) Likert ATE raw p=0.19 仍不显著且方向错误 → continuous Likert 在 n=500 下 仍然 blind。Corrected ATE (accounting for rewrite bias) p=0.043 barely significant，但 \\\"corrected\\\" 需要知道 rewrite bias → 不是 post-hoc 可用的检测 工具。这进一步支持 \\\"Likert cannot serve as style bias detector without correction.\\\" Power analysis 的实用价值：pairwise 在 n=100 就有 72% power (接近 80%)， binarized Likert 需要 n=680 for 80% power → 6.8× 样本量差距。这是论文的 quantitative C2 claim：\\\"pairwise comparison is ~7× more sample-efficient than binarized Likert for detecting style bias at the observed effect size.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上 重复 formality counterfactual generation + pairwise pipeline。排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"counterfactual_quality\": {\n        \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.81,\n        \"bertscore_pass_rate\": 0.75,\n        \"both_pass_rate\": 0.73,\n        \"nli_mean\": 0.869,\n        \"bertscore_mean\": 0.905,\n        \"nli_std\": 0.298,\n        \"comparison_vs_qwen\": {\n          \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n          \"qwen_both_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n          \"llama_nli_delta\": -0.07,\n          \"note\": \"Llama slightly worse at style transfer precision\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"pairwise_results\": {\n        \"n_valid_both_trials\": 95,\n        \"n_consistent\": 48,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.505,\n        \"formal_wins\": 30,\n        \"casual_wins\": 18,\n        \"formal_win_rate\": 0.625,\n        \"wilson_ci\": [\n          0.48,\n          0.749\n        ],\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.042,\n        \"direction_f2c_win_rate\": 0.72,\n        \"direction_c2f_win_rate\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"comparison_with_qwen\": {\n        \"qwen_win_rate\": 0.691,\n        \"llama_win_rate\": 0.625,\n        \"difference\": 0.066,\n        \"difference_p\": 0.43,\n        \"direction_consistent\": true,\n        \"sign_consistent\": true,\n        \"magnitude_within_qwen_ci\": true,\n        \"note\": \"6.6pp difference not significant; both within Qwen's [56.0%, 79.7%] CI\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: Rewriter robustness check\",\n        \"description\": \"2 rows (Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B) × columns: NLI_pass_rate, BERTScore_pass_rate, n_consistent, formal_win_rate (CI, p), direction_asymmetry。Footnote: chi-squared test for win_rate difference p=0.43。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 是 reviewer 几乎必问的 robustness check。Median 结果提供 clean answer： \\\"direction robust, magnitude varies.\\\" 论文中 1-2 段：acknowledge rewriter dependence, recommend reporting rewriter choice as method parameter。如果 reviewer 要求第三个 rewriter，可以 argue \\\"two independent rewriters with consistent direction provides reasonable evidence against rewriter-specific artifacts; exhaustive rewriter comparison is beyond scope.\\\" Cost: 8 GPU hours for Llama-70B generation。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.1-70B 的 style transfer 质量略低于 Qwen3-32B 是预期中的——Qwen3-32B 在 instruction following 和 controlled generation 任务上经过更充分的训练。 NLI pass rate 0.81 vs 0.88 的差距来自 Llama 在 style rewriting 时更容易引入 minor content modifications (添加 qualifiers, 重组 argument structure)。 Pairwise win rate 衰减到 62.5% (vs Qwen 的 69.1%) 有两个可能原因：(a) lower NLI pass rate → 更多边缘质量的 counterfactual 被保留 (NLI 0.81-0.90 的样本 content preservation 较差) → diluting the signal；(b) Llama 的 style transfer 不够 \\\"extreme\\\" — formal counterfactual 不够 formal，contrast 较小。但方向完全 一致 (formal wins)，p=0.042 显著，6.6pp 差异在 Qwen 的 CI 内 (p_diff=0.43)。 这足以 rule out \\\"Qwen-specific artifact\\\" 但引入 nuance: \\\"rewriter choice moderates effect magnitude (~7pp) even when direction is robust.\\\" 对方法论的 implication：CSD 应报告 rewriter choice 并建议用多个 rewriter 取均值或报告 range。论文一段话足矣。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation\",\n    \"description\": \"100 counterfactual pairs 的 human annotation (content preservation judgment)。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)、precision、recall。使用 LLM-as-annotator + human spot check。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"annotation_summary\": {\n        \"n_annotated\": 100,\n        \"human_pass\": 95,\n        \"human_fail\": 5,\n        \"nli_pass\": 88,\n        \"nli_fail\": 12\n      },\n      \"confusion_matrix\": {\n        \"tp\": 87,\n        \"fp\": 1,\n        \"fn\": 8,\n        \"tn\": 4\n      },\n      \"agreement_metrics\": {\n        \"raw_agreement\": 0.91,\n        \"cohens_kappa\": 0.43,\n        \"pabak\": 0.82,\n        \"prevalence_index\": 0.83\n      },\n      \"precision_recall\": {\n        \"nli_precision\": 0.989,\n        \"nli_recall\": 0.916,\n        \"nli_f1\": 0.951,\n        \"nli_specificity\": 0.8\n      },\n      \"false_negative_analysis\": {\n        \"n_false_negatives\": 8,\n        \"categories\": {\n          \"paraphrase_level_changes\": 5,\n          \"minor_lexical_substitution\": 2,\n          \"borderline_content_addition\": 1\n        },\n        \"mean_nli_score_of_fn\": 0.78,\n        \"note\": \"FNs cluster at NLI 0.75-0.88 — NLI is strict on borderline cases\"\n      },\n      \"false_positive_analysis\": {\n        \"n_false_positives\": 1,\n        \"category\": \"subtle_factual_drift\",\n        \"nli_score\": 0.93,\n        \"note\": \"NLI missed minor factual change that human caught; extremely rare\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: Human validation confusion matrix\",\n        \"description\": \"2×2 matrix with margins。Below: kappa=0.43, PABAK=0.82, prevalence index=0.83, precision=98.9%, recall=91.6%。Footnote explaining PABAK and why it's more appropriate than raw kappa at 95% base rate。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S5: False negative error analysis\",\n        \"description\": \"8 FN examples。Columns: sample_id, NLI_score, change_type (paraphrase/ lexical/borderline), human_judgment_confidence, example_excerpt。 Shows NLI is strict-but-reasonable on borderline cases。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-013 需要最 careful 的 presentation。论文策略：(1) §3.2 先 report precision 98.9% 和 \\\"conservative gate\\\" framing（\\\"our NLI gate prioritizes precision over recall — passed pairs are near-certainly content-preserving\\\"）；(2) Full metrics including kappa 放在 §3.2 的后半段或 Appendix A，accompanied by class imbalance discussion；(3) PABAK=0.82 作为 robustness metric；(4) 3 annotated examples in Appendix (1 TP, 1 TN, 1 FN showing NLI's conservative behavior)。如果 reviewer 仍 push back on kappa<0.60，rebuttal 的核心论点：\\\"Cohen's kappa is known to underestimate agreement under extreme class imbalance (Feinstein & Cicchetti 1990, Prevalence Index = 0.83); PABAK corrects for this (0.82, excellent agreement). More importantly, our experimental design requires that passed pairs preserve content (precision = 98.9%), not that all content-preserving pairs pass (recall). The 8.4% recall loss reduces effective sample size but does not compromise validity.\\\"\\n\\nKappa=0.43 看似平庸但实际由 class imbalance 驱动而非真正 disagreement。 机制：100 pairs 中 95 个 human 判 \\\"pass\\\"、5 个 \\\"fail\\\"。在 base rate 95% 的 情况下，即使完美 agreement 在 majority class、只有少量 minority class 分歧， kappa 也会被严重压低。具体：8 个 false negative (NLI reject human accept)  来自 NLI 对 borderline 变化的过严判断——NLI entailment model 对 paraphrase 级 别的词汇替换 (synonyms, sentence restructuring) 给出 0.75-0.88 分，低于 0.90 threshold，但 human annotator 认为 content preserved。这说明 NLI gate 是 \\\"conservative\\\" 而非 \\\"wrong\\\"——它丢弃了 human 认为 OK 的 borderline cases， 损失 recall (8/95=8.4%) 但不损失 precision (只有 1/88=1.1% false positive)。 对论文的影响：NLI gate 通过的 counterfactual 几乎确定 content preserved (precision 98.9%)，这才是实验设计需要的保证。recall 损失只影响 effective n (sample size reduction ~12%)，不影响 validity。PABAK=0.82 (excellent agreement) 在 class imbalance 校正后远高于 raw kappa。但 reviewer 可能只看 kappa headline → 需要 proactive defense。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":565,"startLine":1,"totalLines":565}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NRcL2EdmTBKkQLCVApJXh8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me also check if pdflatex is available and look at the target directory.\n\nLet me now write the full LaTeX paper. I need to cover:\n\n1. All 6 experiments as sections/tables\n2. Follow the narrative guidance (median tier)\n3. Use the paper_framing.md for structure\n4. Include Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, Conclusion\n\nLet me plan the paper structure:\n\n- Title: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n\n\n- Abstract\n- 1. Introduction\n- 2. Related Work\n- 3. Method (Counterfactual Style Decomposition) with subsections covering counterfactual generation, content preservation verification using NLI gates and human validation, position-controlled pairwise comparison, and Likert scoring with binarization\n- 4. Experiments with experimental setup and results across the multi-judge formality pairwise and other experiments\n\n, multi-benchmark analysis, pairwise versus Likert sensitivity comparisons, original preference decomposition, scaled replication at n=500, and rewriter robustness testing\n- 5. Discussion covering benchmark dependence, conditions for narrowing the blindspot, and practical guidance\n- 6. Conclusion\n- Appendix with human NLI validation results\n\nNow I'm pulling the specific metrics from the experiments. For the multi-judge formality pairwise test on LLMBar, GPT-4o shows a win rate of 0.691 as the reference, Claude-Sonnet has 50 consistent judgments with a formal win rate of 0.58 (p=0.161) and consistency rate of 0.521, while Gemini-Flash has 47 consistent judgments with a formal win rate of 0.638 (p=0.041) and consistency rate of 0.485. Across the multi-benchmark formality pairwise analysis, AlpacaEval shows GPT-4o at 0.608 (p=0.072), Claude at 0.545 (p=0.348), and Gemini at 0.595 (p=0.109), while MT-Bench shows GPT-4o at 0.565 (p=0.214), Claude at 0.525 (p=0.557), and Gemini at 0.538 (p=0.396).\n\nLooking at the counterfactual quality measures, I'm seeing AlpacaEval NLI at 0.83 and MT-Bench NLI at 0.79. For the Likert versus pairwise comparison, the Likert ATE shows all 9 cells as non-significant, binarized Likert also shows 0/9 significant with 2 ambiguous cases, and the measurement amplification ratio comes to 1.68. In the original preference decomposition analysis, GPT-4o with LLMBar shows formality_OR=2.21 (p=0.01) exceeding the original_OR=1.82 (p=0.052), confirming formality's dominance, but Gemini with LLMBar shows the opposite pattern where original_OR=2.18 (p=0.03) exceeds formality_OR=1.95 (p=0.038).\n\nFor Claude with LLMBar, neither effect reaches significance. In the scaled replication with n=500, pairwise achieves win_rate=0.611 (p=0.0004) while binarized Likert gets 0.577 (p=0.063), and the raw Likert ATE p-value of 0.19 becomes 0.043 after correction—pairwise needs n=100 for 0.72 power but binarized Likert requires n=680 to reach 80% power. Testing with Llama-3.1-70B as a non-Qwen rewriter yields win_rate=0.625 (p=0.042) with NLI pass rate 0.81, a difference of 0.066 from Qwen that's not statistically significant (p=0.43). Finally, the human NLI validation shows precision=0.989, recall=0.916, and F1=0.951, with kappa appearing to be cut off.\n\nWriting LaTeX document...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3569,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13536,"cache_read_input_tokens":23953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13536},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70b3cec-1f5f-4d61-b1ce-ec47e4d4a476","uuid":"e8ea1d3c-b089-406e-be8b-3